From: NGM <ngm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ngm-compat: keep OPENSSL_ALGO_DSS1 working on OpenSSL >= 1.1

What: on OpenSSL >= 1.1 keep the OPENSSL_ALGO_DSS1 constant and map it to
EVP_sha1(). DSS1 was OpenSSL's name for DSA-with-SHA-1; 1.1 removed the
EVP_dss1() alias, and plain SHA-1 is the same digest (OpenSSL picks the DSA
signature scheme from the key).

Why ours: CloudLinux's php-5.3.29-openssl11.patch (force-kept) follows
upstream 5.6/7.x and drops the constant on OpenSSL >= 1.1. The former
chrismfz/php53 fork kept it, mapped to SHA-1, so 5.3 code calling
openssl_sign()/openssl_verify() with OPENSSL_ALGO_DSS1 worked on our builds;
without this it gets "Use of undefined constant" + "Unknown signature
algorithm" (ext/openssl/tests/bug41033.phpt). This keeps the 5.3 runtime
behaving as it did. 5.6/7.x here match upstream (no DSS1), as before.

Behaviour change: none versus the previous 5.3 build; versus pristine
CloudLinux on OpenSSL 1.1+, OPENSSL_ALGO_DSS1 exists and works.

Delete when: 5.3 is retired, or we decide 5.3 should match upstream.
---
--- a/ext/openssl/openssl.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/openssl.c
@@ -1072,11 +1072,14 @@
 			mdtype = (EVP_MD *) EVP_md2();
 			break;
 #endif
-#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER < 0x10100000L || defined (LIBRESSL_VERSION_NUMBER)
 		case OPENSSL_ALGO_DSS1:
+#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER < 0x10100000L || defined (LIBRESSL_VERSION_NUMBER)
 			mdtype = (EVP_MD *) EVP_dss1();
-			break;
+#else
+			/* DSS1 was DSA-with-SHA-1; OpenSSL 1.1 dropped the alias, SHA-1 is the digest */
+			mdtype = (EVP_MD *) EVP_sha1();
 #endif
+			break;
 		default:
 			return NULL;
 			break;
@@ -1164,9 +1167,7 @@
 #ifdef HAVE_OPENSSL_MD2_H
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("OPENSSL_ALGO_MD2", OPENSSL_ALGO_MD2, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
 #endif
-#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER < 0x10100000L || defined (LIBRESSL_VERSION_NUMBER)
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("OPENSSL_ALGO_DSS1", OPENSSL_ALGO_DSS1, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
-#endif
 
 	/* flags for S/MIME */
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("PKCS7_DETACHED", PKCS7_DETACHED, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
